Module 6: How to Investigate Event 4688 (4688 this is called windows event IDs) => you will study more like this = 4624, 4625, and much more...

Never jump to conclusions.

Always ask:

WHO ?

Which user started it ?

Examples:
Iqrar
SYSTEM
LOCAL SERVICE
NETWORK SERVICE


WHAT ?
Which process started?
Examples:
powershell.exe
cmd.exe
chrome.exe


WHEN ?
Time
Date
Was it during office hours?
Midnight?
Weekend?

WHERE ?
Executable path
Normal:
C:\Windows\System32\

Suspicious:
C:\Users\Public\


WHY ?
Expected behavior?
Or suspicious?


HOW ?
Command line
Parent Process
Child Process
